{#
settings/sharing/_lists.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The response to every mutation in Settings → Sharing: creating, editing,
revoking, regenerating and deleting a share link, and the same five for a
booking page.

One region, redrawn whole, for both halves. That is why CalendarSharingController
is one controller rather than two — a stream that replaced only the links would
leave a newly created booking page invisible until the page was reloaded, which
is exactly the bug calendar/_lists.stream.html.twig exists to prevent.

Variables:
  shareLinks        CalendarShareLink[]
  bookingPages      BookingPage[]
  toastMessage      string       translation key
  mintedLinkUrl     string|null  shown once, then never again
  mintedBookingUrl  string|null  shown once, then never again
#}
<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            message: toastMessage|trans,
            type: 'success',
        } %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>

{# The target id is re-emitted inside its own replacement: a replace whose
   template drops the id works exactly once, and the second stream silently
   does nothing. #}
<turbo-stream action="replace" target="settings-sharing-list">
    <template>
        <div id="settings-sharing-list">
            {% include 'settings/sharing/_lists.html.twig' with {
                shareLinks: shareLinks,
                bookingPages: bookingPages,
                mintedLinkUrl: mintedLinkUrl|default(null),
                mintedBookingUrl: mintedBookingUrl|default(null),
            } only %}
        </div>
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
